course: dictionary
lesson: 1144
title: Words from weddings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bridesmaid is a girl or woman who helps the bride on her wedding day and walks with her at the ceremony. You can work this out from the words around it. «At Mum's wedding Sky is a bridesmaid in a lilac dress» tells you Sky is part of the wedding, and the special dress tells you she is dressed for the day.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Your cousin is a bridesmaid in a matching dress» still makes sense if you swap in "a girl who helps the bride in a matching dress", so your meaning fits.
explain: Some words have a second meaning in a saying. «Always the bridesmaid, never the bride» is not about weddings at all. It means someone always nearly wins but never quite does. The words around the saying tell you which meaning is in use.
fact: A bridesmaid is a girl or woman who helps the bride and walks with her at the ceremony.
fact: The chief bridesmaid, also called the maid of honour, is the main bridesmaid.
fact: A flower girl is a little one at a wedding; page boys are little boys at a wedding too.
fact: A «bridesmaid dress» is the special dress a bridesmaid wears.
fact: The saying «always the bridesmaid, never the bride» means always nearly winning but never quite winning.
exercise: «Your cousin is a bridesmaid in a matching dress.» What is a bridesmaid? | A flower that grows near the church | The person who marries the groom | *A girl or woman who helps the bride on her wedding day | A guest who sings a song at the party
exercise: «At Mum's wedding Sky is a bridesmaid in a lilac dress.» What colour is Sky's dress? | *Lilac | White | Red | Green
exercise: What does the saying «always the bridesmaid, never the bride» mean? | Always wearing white | *Always nearly winning, but never quite winning | Always getting married first | Always the best dancer at a party
test: What is a «maid of honour»? | A little boy who carries the rings | A guest sitting at the back of the hall | *The chief bridesmaid, the main one who helps the bride | The bride's mum
test: «Uncle Dev shakes over his best man's speech.» Whose speech is Uncle Dev nervous about? | *His best man's | The bride's | The flower girl's | Mum's
exam: «Children can be flower girls or page boys.» What is a flower girl? | *A little one at a wedding | The bride's sister who makes the cake | A girl who sells flowers in the street | A grown-up woman who marries the groom
